# cybersecurity-journey
My 12-week practical cybersecurity journey, focused on Network Security and later Identity &amp; Access Management (IAM).
## Personal Reflection

Today I learned the difference between authentication and authorization.

The most important lesson for me was understanding that authentication answers
"Who are you?" while authorization answers "What are you allowed to do?"

I also learned how MFA can reduce the impact of stolen credentials and how
the principle of least privilege limits the damage a compromised account can cause.

### My Mistake Today

I initially confused authentication with authorization when answering the
Day 3 assessment. I learned that a password is used for authentication,
while authorization determines what the authenticated user is permitted to access.

### Next Step

Continue building my cybersecurity fundamentals and begin applying these
concepts in practical environments.
